  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;!--StartFragment--&gt;&lt;span data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;Within two months of the date of this permission, the approved noise and vibration attenuation measures detailed in the submitted Noise Impact Assessment shall be implemented. Following the completion of the proposed mitigation measures, a post-installation acoustic verification report, prepared by a suitably qualified acoustic consultant, shall be submitted to and approved in writing &amp;nbsp;by the Local Planning Authority, The report shall demonstrate that the cumulative operational noise from all fixed plant and machinery complies with the approved noise criterion of at least 10 dB(A) below the representative background noise level (LA90,T) at the nearest noise-sensitive receptor. Where the approved noise limits are not achieved, additional mitigation measures shall be implemented and a further verification report submitted to the Local Planning Authority demonstrating compliance.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;!--EndFragment--&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and documents:",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;PT Sans&amp;quot;,sans-serif&quot;&gt;The cumulative rating noise\r\nlevel from all plant and machinery shall not exceed &lt;strong&gt;10dB(A) below the prevailing\r\nbackground noise level &lt;/strong&gt;(measured in accordance with\r\nBS4142:2014) at the nearest noise-sensitive premises. The plant shall operate\r\n24/7 in compliance with &lt;strong&gt;Harrow\r\nCouncil’s plant noise limits&lt;/strong&gt;, and the developer shall ensure\r\nthat these noise limits are achieved and maintained thereafter through\r\nappropriate monitoring and mitigation measures.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
